{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>בני ישראל אות היא</b> — rashei tevot: ביאה שביאתו של תלמיד חכם מערב שבת לערב שבת. אות היא לעולם כי — rashei tevot: אהלך, as it is written: וידעת כי שלום אהלך, and we derive from it: kindling the lamp on Sabbath eve." "<b>וביום השביעי שבת וינפש</b> — ס\"ת: two. That a man has two souls on Sabbath, and therefore the peh of וינפש is doubled on account of two souls." "<b>וינפש</b> — gematria: אלו שבגיהנם, that even the fire of Gehenna rests on Sabbath." "<b>השביעי שבת וינפש</b> — gematria: דכיון שהוא שבת אבדה נפש." "<b>שבת וינפש ויתן אל</b> משה. Teaches that the Torah was given on Sabbath. וינפש — vav. נפש, and juxtaposed to it is the section of the calf, for they became liable to death and their souls were lost."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The rashei tevot at the end spell אהלך from the initial letters of the three phrases cited; the midrash derives the obligation of Sabbath lamp-kindling from this juxtaposition.", 1 "ס\"ת here refers to the middle letters (סת\"ם) of the cited phrase, which sum or count to two; the doubled letter peh in וינפש signals the two souls.", 2 "The gematria equates וינפש with the phrase אלו שבגיהנם; the specific numeric value is not stated by the author.", 3 "The gematria equates the cited phrase with the phrase דכיון שהוא שבת אבדה נפש; no numeric value is given by the author.", 4 "The author parses וינפש as vav + נפש (soul), then notes the textual juxtaposition of the Sabbath passage to the golden calf narrative."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:58.758520292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}